Anika Patel: Quick ping — dropped a small PR that changes the batching heuristic to prefer shorter prefix windows and tunes KV cache TTL to avoid thrash. Needs a +1 to merge before EOD deploy window. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/runtime/pull/4387
Jonathan Wu: On it, running unit tests locally. will check the fallback path.
CI Bot: build/checks passed — all green (linux, mac, unit, e2e)
Maria Gomez: skimmed — two tiny nits: 1) prefers explicit const on the new param, 2) add a short comment on eviction rationale. otherwise LGTM.
Samir Khan: I can take a proper look in ~30m. does this affect prewarm behavior?
Anika Patel: @Samir yes — I added a small prewarm exception so warmup requests won't increment eviction counters. here's the core change:
```
if (request.isPrewarm()) {
  kv_cache.bump_untracked(request.key);
} else {
  kv_cache.bump(request.key);
}
```
Liz Chen: quick note: this changes the batch size calc for short sequences, validated on toy load and saw 6% p50 improvement.
Jonathan Wu: looked at the kernel callsite — attention kernel tile unchanged. one suggestion: rename param short_seq_bias -> short_seq_boost for clarity. other than that :shipit: 
Anika Patel: updated with Maria's comments + renamed param. PTAL for final.
MergeBot: Merge window opens in 1h. if you need an expedited merge, add `@mergebot expedite`.
Jonathan Wu: approving now.
Samir Khan: approved as well. no perf regressions on my end.
Anika Patel: thanks all — merging in the next window. :tada:
